# Changelog convention

When you make **any notable change** to this project, **update `CHANGELOG.md` in the same change set**.

## When to update

- New features (screens, flows, integrations)
- Bug fixes or behavioral changes
- New or removed dependencies
- Theme, UI, or layout changes
- New utilities, providers, or project structure

## How to update

- Use the existing format: [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/) (Added / Changed / Fixed).
- Add entries under the current version (`## [0.1.0]`) and the appropriate section.
- Be concise but specific (what was added/changed/fixed and where).
- If introducing a new version, add a new `## [x.y.z] – YYYY-MM-DD` section.

## Example

After adding a new "Export" feature:

```markdown
### Added

- **Export**
  - Export transactions to CSV from the Reports screen; file saved to app documents.
```

Do not leave the changelog outdated after implementing user-requested changes.
